    {
      "id": "6hitoro",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Sound"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Sound is a longitudinal mechanical wave that requires a material medium to propagate and cannot travel in a vacuum.",
        "Loudness of sound depends on the amplitude of vibration, whereas pitch depends on the frequency.",
        "An echo is formed by the reflection of sound and requires a minimum distance of 17.2 meters between the source and obstacle.",
        "Ultrasound has frequencies higher than 20,000 Hz and is widely used in medical imaging, SONAR, and industrial cleaning.",
        "The speed of sound is highest in solids, moderate in liquids, and lowest in gases."
      ],
      "id": "n59ouqw"
    },
